concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-21-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21 Applying for variation or revocation of conditions on"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-21-2 ;
    values:originalText "accreditation (1) An accredited entity may apply for a condition imposed on the entity’s accreditation under paragraph 17(2)(a) to be varied or revoked. Note: See Part 5 of Chapter 9 for matters relating to applications. (2) If, after receiving an application under subsection (1), the Digital ID Regulator refuses to vary or revoke a condition, the Digital ID Regulator must give to the entity written notice of the refusal, including reasons for the refusal." ;
    skos:definition "accreditation (1) An accredited entity may apply for a condition imposed on the entity’s accreditation under paragraph 17(2)(a) to be varied or revoked. Note: See Part 5 of Chapter 9 for matters relating to applications. (2) If, after receiving an application under subsection (1), the Digital ID Regulator refuses to vary or revoke a condition, the Digital ID Regulator must give to the entity written notice of the refusal, including reasons for the refusal."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7df3253d5d95627da56a964423854d42743189f3d6bd9896b01f4aa9036f05e4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "37"^^xsd:integer ;
