doc:sec-38-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "38(2) Contraventions of Division 2 and section 136 are interferences" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The respondent to a complaint under the Privacy Act 1988 about the act or practice, other than an act or practice of an agency or organisation, is the entity that engaged in the act or practice." ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-38-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "38(3) Contraventions of Division 2 and section 136 are interferences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-38-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The entity is taken, for the purposes of Part V of the Privacy Act 1988 and any other provision of that Act that relates to that Part, to be an organisation if: (a) the act or practice of the entity that contravenes a provision of Division 2 of this Part or section 136 is the subject of a complaint to, or an investigation by, the Information Commissioner under Part V of the Privacy Act 1988; and (b) the entity is not an agency or organisation." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The entity is taken, for the purposes of Part V of the Privacy Act 1988 and any other provision of that Act that relates to that Part, to be an organisation if: (a) the act or practice of the entity that contravenes a provision of Division 2 of this Part or section 136 is the subject of a complaint to, or an investigation by, the Information Commissioner under Part V of the Privacy Act 1988; and (b) the entity is not an agency or organisation."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "64f8edc2cceb4697feb637e8552873e73e266a2b617a1e4caa9ae102bdea7fcc" ;
    values:partOf concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-38 ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Entity must be considered an organisation if it is subject to a complaint or investigation under Part V of the Privacy Act 1988." ;
