doc:sec-45 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45 Individuals must expressly consent to disclosure of certain" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "attributes of individuals to relying parties When verifying the identity of an individual or authenticating a digital ID of, or information about, an individual to a relying party, an accredited entity must not disclose any of the following attributes of the individual to the relying party without the express consent of the individual: (a) the individual’s current name or former name; (b) the individual’s address; (c) the individual’s date of birth; (d) the individual’s phone number; (e) the individual’s email address; (f) an attribute of a kind prescribed by the Accreditation Rules. Civil penalty: 1,500 penalty units." ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-46 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "46 Disclosure of restricted attributes of individuals"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-46 ;
    values:originalText "(1) When verifying the identity of an individual or authenticating a digital ID of, or information about, an individual to a relying party, an accredited entity must not disclose a restricted attribute of the individual to the relying party without the express consent of the individual. Civil penalty: 1,500 penalty units. (2) An accredited entity must not disclose a restricted attribute of an individual to a relying party that is not a participating relying party if the accredited entity’s conditions on accreditation do not include an authorisation to disclose the restricted attribute to the relying party.  Chapter 3  Privacy" ;
    skos:definition "(1) When verifying the identity of an individual or authenticating a digital ID of, or information about, an individual to a relying party, an accredited entity must not disclose a restricted attribute of the individual to the relying party without the express consent of the individual. Civil penalty: 1,500 penalty units. (2) An accredited entity must not disclose a restricted attribute of an individual to a relying party that is not a participating relying party if the accredited entity’s conditions on accreditation do not include an authorisation to disclose the restricted attribute to the relying party.  Chapter 3  Privacy"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3748d5cbdf0bcf38ed07d9ae5fc7305a6859185c571fade2f22e2c96faa26b3b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
