doc:sec-49-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "49(2) Authorised collection, use and disclosure of biometric" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An accredited entity is authorised to collect, use or disclose biometric information of an individual if:  Privacy  Chapter 3 Privacy  Part 2 Additional privacy safeguards  Division 2 Section 49 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 (a) the biometric information is contained in a verifiable credential that is in the individual’s control; and (b) the Accreditation Rules prescribe requirements relating to the collection, use or disclosure of the biometric information; and (c) the collection, use or disclosure complies with those requirements." ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "49(3) Authorised collection, use and disclosure of biometric"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-49-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information of an individual to a law enforcement agency only if: (a) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by or under a warrant issued under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or (b) the information is disclosed with the express consent of the individual to whom the biometric information relates, or purports to relate, and the disclosure is for the purpose of: (i) verifying the identity of the individual; or (ii) investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory." ;
    skos:definition "(3) An accredited entity is authorised to disclose biometric information of an individual to a law enforcement agency only if: (a) the disclosure of the information is required or authorised by or under a warrant issued under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or (b) the information is disclosed with the express consent of the individual to whom the biometric information relates, or purports to relate, and the disclosure is for the purpose of: (i) verifying the identity of the individual; or (ii) investigating or prosecuting an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5abce120c9978f6eb6cc7bac1ee07517f872a5e8e18b704973040065bb239051" ;
    values:partOf concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-49 ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of biometric information is permitted to law enforcement agencies under certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
