concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-50 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50 Accredited entities may collect etc. biometric information for"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-50 ;
    values:originalText "purposes of government identity documents (1) This section applies if: (a) an accredited entity collects biometric information of an individual under subparagraph 49(1)(b)(i) for the purpose of verifying the identity of the individual; and (b) the accredited entity has verified that the biometric information is legitimate. Note: Because this Chapter applies to an entity only to the extent that the entity is providing accredited services (see section 33), this section does not affect information collected, held etc. by the entity in its capacity as the issuer of the document or other credential. (2) If the entity is covered by subsection (3), the entity may collect, use, disclose or retain the biometric information for the purposes of issuing a document or other credential that: (a) contains personal information about the individual; and (b) the individual has expressly consented to the issue of; and (c) can be used to assist the individual to prove the individual’s age or identity or a permission or authorisation that the individual holds; and  Chapter 3  Privacy" ;
    skos:definition "purposes of government identity documents (1) This section applies if: (a) an accredited entity collects biometric information of an individual under subparagraph 49(1)(b)(i) for the purpose of verifying the identity of the individual; and (b) the accredited entity has verified that the biometric information is legitimate. Note: Because this Chapter applies to an entity only to the extent that the entity is providing accredited services (see section 33), this section does not affect information collected, held etc. by the entity in its capacity as the issuer of the document or other credential. (2) If the entity is covered by subsection (3), the entity may collect, use, disclose or retain the biometric information for the purposes of issuing a document or other credential that: (a) contains personal information about the individual; and (b) the individual has expressly consented to the issue of; and (c) can be used to assist the individual to prove the individual’s age or identity or a permission or authorisation that the individual holds; and  Chapter 3  Privacy"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3c3c85fb6a0a7e51182c7a8f006d7530136ca9ee07299cfc48188597e892e299" ;
    cof:pageNumber "65"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-50-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-50-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <digital-id-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.65" .
