doc:sec-51-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "51(3) Destruction of biometric information of individuals" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subject to subsections (4) and (5), if: (a) an accredited entity collects biometric information of an individual with the express consent of the individual to whom the information relates; and (b) the information is collected for the purposes of authenticating the individual to their digital ID; and (c) the individual withdraws their consent; the accredited entity must destroy the information immediately after the consent is withdrawn." ;
    cof:pageNumber "67"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-51-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "51(4) Destruction of biometric information of individuals"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-51-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If an accredited entity retains biometric information of an individual in accordance with subsection 49(6) (about testing), the accredited entity must destroy the information at the earlier of: (a) the completion of testing the information; and  Chapter 3  Privacy" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If an accredited entity retains biometric information of an individual in accordance with subsection 49(6) (about testing), the accredited entity must destroy the information at the earlier of: (a) the completion of testing the information; and  Chapter 3  Privacy"@en ;
