    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-53-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "53(3) Data profiling to track online behaviour is prohibited" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) However, subsection (1) does not apply if the use or disclosure: (a) is for purposes relating to improving the performance or useability of the entity’s information technology system through which the entity’s accredited services are provided and not for broader business purposes; or (b) is for the purposes of the entity complying with this Act; or (c) is required or authorised by or under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory. Note: A person who wishes to rely on this subsection bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter mentioned in this subsection (see section 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "68"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-54 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54 Certain personal information must not be used or disclosed for"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-54 ;
    values:originalText "prohibited enforcement purposes (1) An accredited entity must not use or disclose personal information of an individual that is in the entity’s possession or control for the purposes of enforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of, an enforcement body unless: (a) the personal information is not biometric information of the individual; and (b) any of the following apply: (i) at the time the information is used or disclosed, the accredited entity is satisfied that the enforcement body has started proceedings against a person for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; (ii) at the time the information is used or disclosed, the accredited entity is satisfied that the enforcement body has started proceedings against a person in relation to a breach of a law imposing a penalty or sanction;  Chapter 3  Privacy" ;
    skos:definition "prohibited enforcement purposes (1) An accredited entity must not use or disclose personal information of an individual that is in the entity’s possession or control for the purposes of enforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of, an enforcement body unless: (a) the personal information is not biometric information of the individual; and (b) any of the following apply: (i) at the time the information is used or disclosed, the accredited entity is satisfied that the enforcement body has started proceedings against a person for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; (ii) at the time the information is used or disclosed, the accredited entity is satisfied that the enforcement body has started proceedings against a person in relation to a breach of a law imposing a penalty or sanction;  Chapter 3  Privacy"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e05e6e544c76b77f8158e5a6c63b70f27ed03b6de54ee6c88a993d8690ba8c45" ;
    cof:pageNumber "69"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Personal information must not be used or disclosed for enforcement purposes unless certain conditions are met." ;
