concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-63 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "63 Approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-63 ;
    values:originalText "System is subject to conditions (1) The approval of an entity to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System is subject to the following conditions (the approval conditions): (a) the conditions set out in subsection 64(1); (b) the conditions (if any) imposed by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 64(2), including as varied under subsection 66(1); (c) the conditions (if any) determined by the Digital ID Rules for the purposes of subsection 64(5). (2) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System must comply with the approval conditions that apply to the entity.  Australian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4 Australian Government Digital ID System  Part 2 Participating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2 Section 64 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 Note: Failure to comply with an approval condition may result in a suspension or revocation of the entity’s approval to participate (see sections 71 and 72)." ;
    skos:definition "System is subject to conditions (1) The approval of an entity to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System is subject to the following conditions (the approval conditions): (a) the conditions set out in subsection 64(1); (b) the conditions (if any) imposed by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 64(2), including as varied under subsection 66(1); (c) the conditions (if any) determined by the Digital ID Rules for the purposes of subsection 64(5). (2) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System must comply with the approval conditions that apply to the entity.  Australian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4 Australian Government Digital ID System  Part 2 Participating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2 Section 64 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 Note: Failure to comply with an approval condition may result in a suspension or revocation of the entity’s approval to participate (see sections 71 and 72)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c8cee048ade5b818576207fdb12e87c1b65890890396860a71ae00db88833d23" ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-63-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-63-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <digital-id-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.82" .
doc:sec-63 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "63 Approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "System is subject to conditions (1) The approval of an entity to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System is subject to the following conditions (the approval conditions): (a) the conditions set out in subsection 64(1); (b) the conditions (if any) imposed by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 64(2), including as varied under subsection 66(1); (c) the conditions (if any) determined by the Digital ID Rules for the purposes of subsection 64(5). (2) An entity that holds an approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System must comply with the approval conditions that apply to the entity.  Australian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4 Australian Government Digital ID System  Part 2 Participating in the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 2 Section 64 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 Note: Failure to comply with an approval condition may result in a suspension or revocation of the entity’s approval to participate (see sections 71 and 72)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer .

