concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-69 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "69 Notice of decision of changes of conditions on approval"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-69 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Digital ID Regulator must give an entity written notice of a decision to impose, vary or revoke a condition on an entity’s approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System. (2) The Digital ID Regulator is not required to give an entity notice of the decision if notice of the condition was given in a notice under subsection 62(5). (3) The notice must: (a) state the condition or the variation, or state that the condition is revoked; and (b) state the day on which the condition, variation or revocation takes effect.  Chapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Digital ID Regulator must give an entity written notice of a decision to impose, vary or revoke a condition on an entity’s approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System. (2) The Digital ID Regulator is not required to give an entity notice of the decision if notice of the condition was given in a notice under subsection 62(5). (3) The notice must: (a) state the condition or the variation, or state that the condition is revoked; and (b) state the day on which the condition, variation or revocation takes effect.  Chapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e899eefd831dcc2c6876dde457f5437f6445468a944cf26bd02253634d4d34f5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "89"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-69-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-69-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-69-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <digital-id-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.89" .
doc:sec-69 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "69 Notice of decision of changes of conditions on approval" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Digital ID Regulator must give an entity written notice of a decision to impose, vary or revoke a condition on an entity’s approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System. (2) The Digital ID Regulator is not required to give an entity notice of the decision if notice of the condition was given in a notice under subsection 62(5). (3) The notice must: (a) state the condition or the variation, or state that the condition is revoked; and (b) state the day on which the condition, variation or revocation takes effect.  Chapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System" ;
    cof:pageNumber "89"^^xsd:integer .

