concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-74 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "74 Creating and using a digital ID is voluntary"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-74 ;
    values:originalText "Creating and using a digital ID is voluntary (1) A participating relying party must not, as a condition of providing a service or access to a service, require an individual to create or use a digital ID. Note: The effect of this subsection is that a participating relying party that provides a service, or access to a service, must provide another means of accessing that service that does not involve the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System. (1A) A participating relying party is taken to contravene subsection (1) if: (a) the participating relying party provides the service, or access to the service, by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (b) either of the following apply: (i) the other means is not reasonably accessible; (ii) using the other means results in the service being provided on substantially less favourable terms. Exceptions (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a service of a participating relying party if: (a) the service provides access to another service; and (b) the individual can access the other service by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (c) the other means is reasonably accessible; and  Chapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System" ;
    skos:definition "Creating and using a digital ID is voluntary (1) A participating relying party must not, as a condition of providing a service or access to a service, require an individual to create or use a digital ID. Note: The effect of this subsection is that a participating relying party that provides a service, or access to a service, must provide another means of accessing that service that does not involve the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System. (1A) A participating relying party is taken to contravene subsection (1) if: (a) the participating relying party provides the service, or access to the service, by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (b) either of the following apply: (i) the other means is not reasonably accessible; (ii) using the other means results in the service being provided on substantially less favourable terms. Exceptions (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a service of a participating relying party if: (a) the service provides access to another service; and (b) the individual can access the other service by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (c) the other means is reasonably accessible; and  Chapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e0b31de8e85a8012f1fc57c804f4e345c1c75e1e936c55b65485ea2c5afc1635" ;
    cof:pageNumber "97"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-74-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-74-ss-1a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-74-ss-2 ;
