    values:originalText "(1A) A participating relying party is taken to contravene subsection (1) if: (a) the participating relying party provides the service, or access to the service, by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (b) either of the following apply: (i) the other means is not reasonably accessible; (ii) using the other means results in the service being provided on substantially less favourable terms. Exceptions" ;
    skos:definition "(1A) A participating relying party is taken to contravene subsection (1) if: (a) the participating relying party provides the service, or access to the service, by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (b) either of the following apply: (i) the other means is not reasonably accessible; (ii) using the other means results in the service being provided on substantially less favourable terms. Exceptions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "98d23aa68d68b05f0d452c74928c85a4f5eac0efc14f117b1580db8d856fcbf8" ;
    values:partOf concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-74 ;
