doc:sec-74-ss-1a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "74(1A) Creating and using a digital ID is voluntary" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1A) A participating relying party is taken to contravene subsection (1) if: (a) the participating relying party provides the service, or access to the service, by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (b) either of the following apply: (i) the other means is not reasonably accessible; (ii) using the other means results in the service being provided on substantially less favourable terms. Exceptions" ;
    cof:pageNumber "97"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-74-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "74(2) Creating and using a digital ID is voluntary"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-74-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a service of a participating relying party if: (a) the service provides access to another service; and (b) the individual can access the other service by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (c) the other means is reasonably accessible; and  Chapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System" ;
    skos:definition "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a service of a participating relying party if: (a) the service provides access to another service; and (b) the individual can access the other service by means other than the creation or use of a digital ID through the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (c) the other means is reasonably accessible; and  Chapter 4  Australian Government Digital ID System"@en ;
