    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the interoperability obligation means: (a) the obligation on participating relying parties to provide individuals with a choice of accredited identity service providers when the individual seeks to verify their identity or authenticate their digital ID or other information; and (b) the obligation on accredited entities participating in the Australian Government Digital ID System to provide their accredited services to other entities participating in the system." ;
