doc:sec-81-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "81(2) Entities may conduct testing in the Australian Government" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The authorisation: (a) must be in writing; and (b) must specify the period for which it is in force, which must not exceed 3 months; and (c) may be granted unconditionally or subject to conditions. Note: The System Administrator may vary or revoke the authorisation: see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-81-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "81(3) Entities may conduct testing in the Australian Government"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-81-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If an authorisation under this section is given subject to a condition and the condition is not met at a particular time, the authorisation ceases to be in force at that time.  Australian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4 Australian Government Digital ID System  Part 2 Other matters relating to the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 5 Section 82 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025" ;
    skos:definition "(3) If an authorisation under this section is given subject to a condition and the condition is not met at a particular time, the authorisation ceases to be in force at that time.  Australian Government Digital ID System  Chapter 4 Australian Government Digital ID System  Part 2 Other matters relating to the Australian Government Digital ID System  Division 5 Section 82 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0905ce91f905125a158634e7644562b37272db15905786558322cfc6d98ad9a7" ;
    values:partOf concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-81 ;
