doc:sec-115-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "115(2) Arrangements relating to staff" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) When performing services for the Digital ID Data Standards Chair, the staff are subject to the directions of the Chair.  Trustmarks and registers  Chapter 8 Introduction  Part 1  Section 116 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 Chapter 8—Trustmarks and registers" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-116 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "116 Simplified outline of this Chapter"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-116 ;
    values:originalText "The Digital ID Rules may set out marks, symbols, logos or designs (called digital ID trustmarks) that may or must be used by accredited entities and participating relying parties. An entity may be liable to a civil penalty if the entity: (a) uses a digital ID trustmark and the entity is not authorised by the Digital ID Rules to do so; or (b) is required by the Digital ID Rules to display a digital ID trustmark in circumstances specified in the Digital ID Rules and the entity fails to comply with the requirement. The Digital ID Regulator must establish and maintain the Digital ID Accredited Entities Register, which is a register of entities that are, or have been, accredited entities. The Digital ID Regulator must also establish and maintain the AGDIS Register, which is a register of entities that are approved to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System.  Chapter 8  Trustmarks and registers" ;
    skos:definition "The Digital ID Rules may set out marks, symbols, logos or designs (called digital ID trustmarks) that may or must be used by accredited entities and participating relying parties. An entity may be liable to a civil penalty if the entity: (a) uses a digital ID trustmark and the entity is not authorised by the Digital ID Rules to do so; or (b) is required by the Digital ID Rules to display a digital ID trustmark in circumstances specified in the Digital ID Rules and the entity fails to comply with the requirement. The Digital ID Regulator must establish and maintain the Digital ID Accredited Entities Register, which is a register of entities that are, or have been, accredited entities. The Digital ID Regulator must also establish and maintain the AGDIS Register, which is a register of entities that are approved to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System.  Chapter 8  Trustmarks and registers"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f2794c297c064991277abba37139d4eaf2490e5ef463089e13238a29745fbe01" ;
    cof:pageNumber "129"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Using digital ID trustmark without authorization is prohibited." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <digital-id-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.129" ;
