doc:sec-136 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "136 Destruction or de-identification of certain information" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to: (a) accredited entities that hold an approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System; and (b) accredited entities whose approval to participate in the Australian Government Digital ID System is suspended; and  Chapter 9  Administration" ;
    cof:pageNumber "151"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "137 Reviewable decisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-137 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A decision referred to in column 1 of an item of the following table is a reviewable decision. An entity referred to in column 2 of the item is the affected entity for the decision. Reviewable decisions Item Column 1 Reviewable decision Column 2 Affected entity A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under section 15 to refuse to accredit an entity as an accredited entity (other than on the ground referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a)) The entity who made the application A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under paragraph 17(2)(a) to impose a condition on an entity’s accreditation The entity on whom the condition is imposed A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 17(2) to refuse to impose, on application by an entity, a condition on the entity’s accreditation The entity who made the application A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 20(1) to vary, on the Digital ID Regulator’s own initiative, the conditions imposed on an entity’s accreditation The entity on whom the conditions are imposed A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 20(1) to refuse to vary, on application by an accredited entity, the conditions imposed on the entity’s accreditation The entity who made the application A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 25(2) to suspend the The accredited entity  Chapter 9  Administration" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A decision referred to in column 1 of an item of the following table is a reviewable decision. An entity referred to in column 2 of the item is the affected entity for the decision. Reviewable decisions Item Column 1 Reviewable decision Column 2 Affected entity A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under section 15 to refuse to accredit an entity as an accredited entity (other than on the ground referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a)) The entity who made the application A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under paragraph 17(2)(a) to impose a condition on an entity’s accreditation The entity on whom the condition is imposed A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 17(2) to refuse to impose, on application by an entity, a condition on the entity’s accreditation The entity who made the application A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 20(1) to vary, on the Digital ID Regulator’s own initiative, the conditions imposed on an entity’s accreditation The entity on whom the conditions are imposed A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 20(1) to refuse to vary, on application by an accredited entity, the conditions imposed on the entity’s accreditation The entity who made the application A decision by the Digital ID Regulator under subsection 25(2) to suspend the The accredited entity  Chapter 9  Administration"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "54170077b5fe315f5145f717c97b7e616e7ee681459e34409bd931c3ee40d106" ;
    cof:pageNumber "153"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A decision by the Digital ID Regulator is a reviewable decision." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <digital-id-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.153" ;
    cml:asserts concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-137-norm .
