doc:sec-141-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "141(3) Requirements for applications" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) To avoid doubt, approval may be given for: (a) different forms for different kinds of applications; or (b) a single form for more than one kind of application." ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-142 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "142 Powers in relation to applications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-142 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a person (the applicant) makes an application under this Act, the person to whom the application is made may, by written notice, require the applicant to give the person such further information or documents in relation to the application as the person reasonably requires.  Administration  Chapter 9 Applications under this Act  Part 5  Section 143 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 Note 1: The person is not required to make a decision on the application if this subsection is not complied with (see section 143). Note 2: The Digital ID Regulator may also require an applicant to undergo a compliance assessment before making a decision on the application (see section 131). (2) A notice under subsection (1) may specify a period, which must not be less than 14 days, within which the information or documents must be given." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a person (the applicant) makes an application under this Act, the person to whom the application is made may, by written notice, require the applicant to give the person such further information or documents in relation to the application as the person reasonably requires.  Administration  Chapter 9 Applications under this Act  Part 5  Section 143 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 Note 1: The person is not required to make a decision on the application if this subsection is not complied with (see section 143). Note 2: The Digital ID Regulator may also require an applicant to undergo a compliance assessment before making a decision on the application (see section 131). (2) A notice under subsection (1) may specify a period, which must not be less than 14 days, within which the information or documents must be given."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4c47a9c6decda20766d9d86d9c29b1c68e8356defbd8e1e2f26ba5ca2fce008e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer ;
