doc:sec-149 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "149 Simplified outline of this Chapter" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Minister may establish advisory committees to provide advice to the following in relation to matters arising under this Act: (a) the Minister; (b) the Secretary; (c) the Digital ID Data Standards Chair. A person commits an offence if the person obtains certain kinds of information in the course of, or for the purposes of, performing functions or exercising powers under this Act and the person uses or discloses the information. There are some exceptions. This Chapter also deals with matters of an administrative nature, including: (a) annual reports by the Digital ID Regulator, the Information Commissioner, law enforcement agencies, enforcement bodies and the AFP Minister; and (b) delegations; and (c) rule-making powers.  Other matters  Chapter 10 Advisory committees  Part 2  Section 150 Digital ID Act 2024 Compilation date: 21/02/2025" ;
    cof:pageNumber "164"^^xsd:integer .

concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-150 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "150 Advisory committees"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-150 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may establish, in writing, such advisory committees as the Minister considers appropriate to provide advice to the following in relation to matters arising under this Act, including but not limited to the performance of the Digital ID Regulator’s functions and exercise of the Digital ID Regulator’s powers under this Act: (a) the Minister; (b) the Secretary; (c) the System Administrator; (d) the Digital ID Data Standards Chair. (2) An advisory committee is to consist of such persons as the Minister determines. (3) If the Minister establishes an advisory committee under subsection (1), the Minister must, in writing, determine: (a) the committee’s terms of reference; and (b) the terms and conditions of appointment of the members of the committee, including: (i) term of office; and (ii) remuneration; and (iii) allowances; and (iv) leave of absence; and (v) disclosure of interests; and (vi) termination of membership; and (c) the procedures to be followed by the committee. (4) An instrument made under subsection (1) or (3) is not a legislative instrument.  Chapter 10  Other matters" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may establish, in writing, such advisory committees as the Minister considers appropriate to provide advice to the following in relation to matters arising under this Act, including but not limited to the performance of the Digital ID Regulator’s functions and exercise of the Digital ID Regulator’s powers under this Act: (a) the Minister; (b) the Secretary; (c) the System Administrator; (d) the Digital ID Data Standards Chair. (2) An advisory committee is to consist of such persons as the Minister determines. (3) If the Minister establishes an advisory committee under subsection (1), the Minister must, in writing, determine: (a) the committee’s terms of reference; and (b) the terms and conditions of appointment of the members of the committee, including: (i) term of office; and (ii) remuneration; and (iii) allowances; and (iv) leave of absence; and (v) disclosure of interests; and (vi) termination of membership; and (c) the procedures to be followed by the committee. (4) An instrument made under subsection (1) or (3) is not a legislative instrument.  Chapter 10  Other matters"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6be1b905e6ccb4b8ea6bc1c784e295ea36a6be637cd918285eadcf0538431061" ;
    cof:pageNumber "165"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-150-ss-1 ;
