concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "154 Annual report by the Digital ID Regulator"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-154 ;
    values:originalText "(1) After the end of each financial year, the Digital ID Regulator must prepare and give a report to the Minister, for presentation to the Parliament, on the Digital ID Regulator’s activities during the financial year. (2) The report must include the following: (a) information about the operation of the accreditation scheme, including: (i) the number of applications for accreditation made under section 14; and (ii) the number of accreditations granted under section 15; (b) information about the operation of the Australian Government Digital ID System, including: (i) the number of applications made to participate in the system under section 61; and (ii) the number of approvals granted to participate in the system under section 62; and (iii) the number of digital ID fraud incidents or cyber security incidents, and the responses to any such incidents; (c) information on any other matters notified by the Minister to the Digital ID Regulator. (3) The report must be given to the Minister by: (a) the 30th day of October; or (b) the end of any further period granted under subsection 34C(5) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  Chapter 10  Other matters" ;
    skos:definition "(1) After the end of each financial year, the Digital ID Regulator must prepare and give a report to the Minister, for presentation to the Parliament, on the Digital ID Regulator’s activities during the financial year. (2) The report must include the following: (a) information about the operation of the accreditation scheme, including: (i) the number of applications for accreditation made under section 14; and (ii) the number of accreditations granted under section 15; (b) information about the operation of the Australian Government Digital ID System, including: (i) the number of applications made to participate in the system under section 61; and (ii) the number of approvals granted to participate in the system under section 62; and (iii) the number of digital ID fraud incidents or cyber security incidents, and the responses to any such incidents; (c) information on any other matters notified by the Minister to the Digital ID Regulator. (3) The report must be given to the Minister by: (a) the 30th day of October; or (b) the end of any further period granted under subsection 34C(5) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  Chapter 10  Other matters"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e682a1da4c515fa8ddcbcc55b307fd90fc2bec5dcea6bd50040810b995b7b59d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "169"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:digital-id-act-2024-sec-154-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <digital-id-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "digital-id-act-2024.pdf, p.169" .
doc:sec-154 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "154 Annual report by the Digital ID Regulator" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) After the end of each financial year, the Digital ID Regulator must prepare and give a report to the Minister, for presentation to the Parliament, on the Digital ID Regulator’s activities during the financial year. (2) The report must include the following: (a) information about the operation of the accreditation scheme, including: (i) the number of applications for accreditation made under section 14; and (ii) the number of accreditations granted under section 15; (b) information about the operation of the Australian Government Digital ID System, including: (i) the number of applications made to participate in the system under section 61; and (ii) the number of approvals granted to participate in the system under section 62; and (iii) the number of digital ID fraud incidents or cyber security incidents, and the responses to any such incidents; (c) information on any other matters notified by the Minister to the Digital ID Regulator. (3) The report must be given to the Minister by: (a) the 30th day of October; or (b) the end of any further period granted under subsection 34C(5) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  Chapter 10  Other matters" ;
    cof:pageNumber "169"^^xsd:integer .

